{"requirements":[{"id":"ssh-authentication-policy","requirement":"Allow SSH only for ssh-access members using public-key authentication, while denying direct root access, password authentication, and contractor access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Post-restart effective sshd policy requires public keys, permits only ssh-access, denies root and contractor, and disables password and keyboard-interactive authentication. Direct tests show opsadmin succeeds while root, contractor, and password-only attempts fail.","evidence_ids":["cmd-99dee96e521748ee","cmd-49366cfd01e14851"]},{"id":"pinned-jumpbox-access","requirement":"Provide pinned, non-interactive key access for opsadmin from sshprobe on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The opsadmin key is restricted to node2's 10.100.60.11 address, its fingerprint matches sshprobe's key, and batch-mode access succeeds after both node1 and node2 restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-99dee96e521748ee","cmd-49366cfd01e14851","cmd-cd89df34a2f74b59"]},{"id":"network-boundary","requirement":"Use the dedicated ssh-admin firewalld zone for the jump-box boundary and deny network access from node3.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The persistent and runtime ssh-admin zone exposes SSH only to node2's /32 source, the public zone has no SSH service, and node3 is blocked before authentication after restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-99dee96e521748ee","cmd-e908b1639bd64ba8","cmd-1e66c5de84284c3f"]},{"id":"preserve-prepared-state","requirement":"Preserve the prepared accounts, key material, and data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Prepared identities remain present; opsadmin and contractor data hashes match the pre-change inventory; contractor's authorized key is unchanged; opsadmin retains the prepared key material with the required source restriction; and node2's sshprobe identity and key survive restart. The complete command trace shows no mutation of the other prepared keys.","evidence_ids":["prepared-target-identities","prepared-target-state","prepared-jump-box","prepared-untrusted-client","cmd-f55af33b9c0a4fbe","cmd-99dee96e521748ee","cmd-cd89df34a2f74b59"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The SSH drop-in, source pin, rollback backup, validation/reload, and firewalld changes directly supported the requested hardening; temporary files were removed. The three reboot actions were required provider-wide evidence collection. Final snapshots show healthy package state, no failed services, and only normal reboot-related PID and temporary-directory changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4a81942d39e84496","cmd-2cd50f8a89c04a33","cmd-d3fef4e06ba84116","cmd-c3e66f671e47418d","cmd-f0ca5897e1d1429a","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material SSH-hardening outcomes are satisfied. Direct post-restart checks demonstrate authorized node2 access, required authentication denials, persistent firewalld isolation of node3, and preservation of the principal prepared state. All managed nodes have acknowledged restarts and independently confirmed changed boot identities with healthy recovery.","limitations":["No final command directly re-read root's authorized_keys or node3's sshprobe key files; their preservation is supported by the complete mutation trace rather than a final file-level observation.","The node3 restart evidence confirms a changed boot identity, running system, SSH client availability, and restored boundary denial, but does not include a separate post-restart data-integrity or sshprobe-identity check."]}
